body:
@driesvints Sorry about the confusion. The issue is both.

Signing and verification use different methods to construct the URL. This causes the issue that @jelib3an described, that signed URLs are always invalid if they contain query parameters without a value. It also causes the issue that a URL that is valid (since it did not contain key-only query string parameters) is still valid after tampering with the URL (by adding such parameters).

My solution above intends to resolve both these problems.

use in service provider 

```
Paginator::queryStringResolver(function` () {
            $query = $this->app['request']->query();
            array_walk_recursive($query, function (&$value) {
                if ($value === null) {
                    $value = '';
                }
            });
            return $query;
        });
```
